From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Willmer <info@jwillmer.de>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:18:17 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 113/116] Drag the sidebar's right edge to resize it

A strip at the right edge of the sidebar (the project file tree) shows
a resize pointer and drags the sidebar wider or narrower, like the
divider between two views. The strip takes the place of the sidebar's
right padding, so the sidebar looks the same until it is dragged; until
then it keeps the upstream width (as wide as its items, at most 280 px).
A dragged width stays between 160 px and half the window and is kept in
the session (sidebar_width). A condensed window has no strip. New
src/sidebar.rs with tests.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

